{{$NEXT}}

  - bin/itm_read_simple no longer imports Term::ANSIColor and drops its
    unused color list; it now behaves like itm_read_nocolor and starts
    without Term::ANSIColor installed
  - bin/itm_read_simple POD no longer promises colored output
  - t/scripts.t runs both shipped readers over the same packet stream
  - AnyEvent::ITM::_print_ts and AnyEvent::ITM->_run_cmd are now the
    public, documented print_ts and run_cmd; both shipped readers use the
    new names, the old underscore names are gone
  - t/run_cmd.t checks the exit code and signal that run_cmd reports
  - lib/AnyEvent/ITM.pm, bin/itm_read_simple and bin/itm_read_nocolor
    now declare their own $VERSION (0.002), all the same
  - the hand-written SUPPORT sections are gone from the POD of all three
    files; the release bundle generates them, with the channel #hardware
    now set through irc in dist.ini
  - t/version.t checks the $VERSION of every file under lib/ and bin/ and
    that no POD carries a SUPPORT section
